  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 2be9535df9fadce4d9fc0e46ba83a908, type: 3}
  m_Name: Customer_Sprout
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::WeatherForSale.Shop.CustomerData
  displayName: Sprout
  prefab: {fileID: 769049279164885057, guid: 50f81f913ffd7854eb0fd114a12b934c, type: 3}
  weatherWord: wind
  correctMapId: valley
  problemLine: My kite just won't fly! I need something to lift it back up into the
    sky!
  hintsVague:
  - The air here is so still, my kite just flops on the grass.
  - I ran all the way down the street and it still wouldn't lift. It needs something
    to push it up!
  - Even the flags in town hang down like wet socks. Nothing moves at all.
  hintsNarrow:
  - Grandpa says there's a place where tall orange rocks stand in rows, and the air
    rushes between them so hard your hat flies off.
  - He says the air squeezes through the gaps between the cliffs there and comes
    out whistling like a kettle.
  - His kite once flew so high there it took him a whole afternoon to reel it back
    in!
  hintsClear:
  - Look for tall orange rock towers with little trees on top, standing over a deep
    drop full of clouds.
  - On your map there are white swirly lines curling between the cliffs. That's air
    that never sits still!
  - Grandpa says you can't even see the bottom there, just soft fluffy mist far below
    the rock towers.
  - On your map it's the bottom-left corner, with flat-topped stone towers and twisting
    white streaks.
  thankYouLine: Whoosh! Look at my kite go! Thank you so much!
